{
    "background_story": "Cali grew up in a small town where the local post office was the hub of the community. As a child, she would often accompany her grandmother to the post office, watching as she carefully selected stamps and wrote letters to loved ones. This sparked a fascination with the art of correspondence, and Cali went on to become a postal worker herself. She took great pride in ensuring that every piece of mail reached its destination, often going above and beyond to deliver packages to remote areas. Cali's love for mail wasn't just about the job \u2013 she was a collector of rare stamps and had a passion for letter-writing. She even started a pen pal program for local kids, teaching them the value of handwritten communication in a digital age.",
